<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
  <!--
    This app's own style-class declarations — the consumer-side twin of the theme library's file.

    Any project that defines classes inside its own ControlThemes needs one of these, because that
    shape is invisible to static analysis: `^` only means the control by virtue of the enclosing
    ControlTheme's key. Without it, Classes="hero" below would be underlined "Style class 'hero' not
    found" despite working perfectly.

    Nothing here is written by hand. AngelSix.ThemeEngine ships a build target that walks this
    project's ControlThemes and fills in the region between the markers — create the file with the
    markers in it and that is the whole setup. Note the theme library's own declarations are a
    separate file: each project declares what it defines.

    Still needs including from App.axaml, which is the one step that cannot be automated — a Styles
    subclass loaded by AvaloniaXamlLoader is a type reference an analyser cannot follow into, so
    only a StyleInclude in the consuming XAML is a path it can walk.
  -->

  <!-- BEGIN GENERATED — written by AngelSix.ThemeEngine on build; hand edits here are overwritten -->

  <!-- hero -->
  <Style Selector="Button.hero" />

  <!-- quiet -->
  <Style Selector="Button.quiet" />

  <!-- END GENERATED -->

</Styles>
